"Badud privately finds kingdom-building boring and longs for a worthy rival."
"Nathan's summoning is later counted the work of Badud's lackeys."
"Later, Badud returns to Giantsrest, takes Dennar's office, and hopes Nathan is a Questor."
"He offers Taeol [Mass Teleport] Insights to recapture Nathan."
"Later, he sets Taeol and Nathan up as rivals; Nathan kills Taeol days after."
"Later, Badud leads an army to retake Halsmet and conquer Gemore, meaning then to face Agmon."
"In a mountain pass he kills Brox with a ring of [Quenfi's Hatred], and takes a blade in his gut."
"Later, he casts [Reverse Time] outside Halsmet; Nathan keeps his memory through it."
"In Giantsrest he abducts Nathan's friends, fires the [Last Arrow of Olita], and levels the Academy."
"Nathan breaks his wizardry and kills him there; Badud respawns without his automagic."
"He then trades three continents and 1500 years of non-interference for an early Ending."
"That deal brings Gemore's Ending of History within a century."
"He rules as Archlord of Sangrad from its Seal Fortress and plots to sink Nathan's ship."
"Years later, in Esebus, he attacks the Heirs with radiation and stone; Sarah shoots him dead."
"Later, in the Ostren war, he demands antimagic be banned and vanishes in his own spell."
"At the Conclave, Nathan cripples his magic and kills him a fourth time."
"Nine years after, Badud fights for the Severance Bloc against the Continuance Council."
